# JavaScript docs

- Document every exported function, class, and typedef with JSDoc.
- Type public values with `@typedef`, `@param`, `@returns`, and `@type`. Prefer named typedefs that match `graph.json` over untyped object literals.
- Mark nullable fields with `?` or `| null` so they match the JSON contract (`sourceUrl`, `subtitle`).
- Keep comments to contracts and non-obvious behaviour. Do not restate the identifier.

```javascript
// ❌ BAD
function colourFor(node, mode) {
  return mode === "own" ? node.status : node.rollupStatus;
}

// ✅ GOOD
/**
 * @typedef {object} GraphNode
 * @property {string} id
 * @property {string} status
 * @property {string} rollupStatus
 */

/**
 * Status id used to colour a node in the current mode.
 * @param {GraphNode} node
 * @param {"own" | "rollup"} colorMode
 * @returns {string}
 */
function statusIdForColor(node, colorMode) {
  return colorMode === "own" ? node.status : node.rollupStatus;
}
```
